   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ מַאן תְּנָא? אָמַר רַב אַדָּא בַּר אַהֲבָה: רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר הִיא, דְּתַנְיָא רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר אוֹמֵר: אֲפִילּוּ וִיתּוּר אָסוּר בְּמוּדַּר הֲנָאָה.",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» «Who is the tanna» who taught this mishna? «Rav Adda bar Ahava said: It is Rabbi Eliezer, as it is taught» in a baraita that «Rabbi Eliezer said: Even overlooking [vittur]» a matter for which one is typically indifferent to the actions of others, e.g., people setting foot on one’s property, «is prohibited in» the case of «one prohibited by vow from deriving benefit» from another."
  }
